==French==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|fr|fro|compaing}}, {{m|fro|compain}}, from {{inh|fr|LL.|compāniō}} (nominative form) (compare also {{cog|it|compagno}}), from {{af|la|com-|pānis|nocat=1|lit=with-bread}}, a word first attested in the {{der|fr|frk|-}} ''Lex Salica'' as a translation of a {{der|fr|gem|-}} word, probably {{der|fr|frk|*galaibo}}, {{m|gmw-pro|*gahlaibo||messmate|lit=with-bread}}, from {{m|gmw-pro|*hlaib||loaf, bread}}. See also {{m|fr|compagnon}}, from the accusative form of the same Late Latin term (''compāniōnem''), whence English {{m|en|companion}}. The sense of 'boyfriend' is by ellipsis of {{m|fr|petit copain}}.

